course: dictionary
lesson: 9513
title: A stickleback is a fish, not a stick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A stickleback is a small fish with sharp spines on its back. You can use the clues in the word and the sentences around it to work out what it means. The word begins with stick, but the sentences show it is an animal.
explain: «A pond food chain can be tiny green algae, water fleas, sticklebacks, then a heron or a pike.» Sticklebacks come between water fleas and herons, so they are part of the food chain, and they are living things. Swap in your meaning, a small fish, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «A male stickleback glues weed together with a sticky thread, turns red in spring, guards the eggs and fans water over them.» These words show what a stickleback does. When you read about a new animal, ask what it does, where it lives and what it looks like.
fact: A stickleback is a small fish with sharp spines on its back.
fact: Sticklebacks live in ponds, streams and coastal waters of the Northern Hemisphere.
fact: The male three-spined stickleback builds a nest of plants and turns red underneath in the breeding season.
fact: «Stickleback» is a noun: one stickleback, many sticklebacks.
fact: On a pond dipping trip, catch sticklebacks in a net, look at them, then put them back.
exercise: What is a stickleback? | A type of pond weed | *A small fish with sharp spines on its back | A plant that grows in streams | A small bird that sings in ponds
exercise: In «A male stickleback glues weed together», what is the male building? | A boat | A cave | *A nest | A web
exercise: Which word in «a pond food chain can be tiny green algae, water fleas, sticklebacks, then a heron or a pike» names a fish? | Algae | *Sticklebacks | Water fleas | Heron
test: Where do sticklebacks live? | *In ponds, streams and coastal waters | In deserts | Only in the sea | In trees
test: What does the male stickleback do in the breeding season? | He grows wings and flies away | He hides in a cave | He sings to the other fish | *He turns red underneath and builds a nest of plants
exam: Sam says a stickleback is a kind of stick you can use to dig. Which fact shows he is wrong? | A stickleback has leaves and roots | A stickleback is sold in shops for gardens | A stickleback is a long piece of wood | *A stickleback is a small fish that lives in ponds and streams
